<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ribat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A ribat was a fortified religious community or frontier stronghold in the Islamic world, combining military defence with devotion and study. The Almoravid movement grew from a ribat founded by the preacher Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allah">Allah</a> ibn Yasin among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lamtuna">Lamtuna</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berbers">Berbers</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> profile, the name al-Murabitun, meaning those from the ribat, was rendered by Europeans as Almoravids.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ribat.jpg" alt="Ribat" width="279" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GIRAUD Patrick · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:TUNISIE_MONASTIR_RIBAT_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
